  "body": "<div align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"https://cdn.tw93.fun/pic/cole.png\" alt=\"Mole Logo\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" style=\"border-radius:50%\" />\n  <h1 style=\"margin: 12px 0 6px;\">Mole</h1>\n  <p><em>Deep clean and optimize your Mac.</em></p>\n</div>\n\n### Changelog\n\n1. **Optimize is gentler**: it no longer rebuilds LaunchServices, which dropped VPN tunnels and sent Siri re-indexing, and it only reports LaunchAgents whose program is missing instead of deleting them.\n2. **Clean leaves Gemini's Google state alone**: deleting it while Gemini ran could start a disk write loop of about 50 MB/s.\n3. **Homebrew old versions are cleaned and previewed**: `mo clean` runs `brew cleanup` even with a small download cache, and `mo clean --dry-run` lists each version it would remove.\n4. **A slow check no longer stops the whole run**: a timed-out size or SQLite check now affects only that item.\n5. **Previews and totals count only what goes**: nested items count once, Docker images in use no longer read as reclaimable, and tiny build-artifact hints stay quiet.\n6. **Smaller fixes**: idle Brave Nightly caches are cleaned while another channel runs, VS Code extension cleanup works on macOS 15 again, `mo remove` keeps a custom config directory, and Status shows one more busy process.\n\n### 更新日志\n\n1. **Optimize 更克制**：不再重建 LaunchServices，避免 VPN 断线和 Siri 反复索引，程序缺失的 LaunchAgent 也改为只报告不删除。\n2. **Clean 不再动 Gemini 的 Google 身份数据**：Gemini 运行时删掉它们会触发每秒约 50 MB 的持续写盘。\n3. **Homebrew 旧版本能清理也能预览**：下载缓存很小时 `mo clean` 也会执行 `brew cleanup`，`mo clean --dry-run` 会逐个列出将删除的版本。\n4. **单项检查超时不再中断整轮清理**：体积或 SQLite 检查超时只影响这一项，其余照常进行。\n5. **预览和汇总只算真正会清掉的部分**：嵌套项只算一次，正在使用的 Docker 镜像不再算作可回收，很小的构建产物也不再提示。\n6. **其他细节修复**：另一个 Brave 渠道开着时也能清理空闲的 Nightly 缓存，VS Code 旧扩展清理在 macOS 15 上恢复正常，`mo remove` 会保留自定义配置目录，Status 进程卡片多显示一个进程。\n\n### Thanks\n\nIssue reporters and PR contributors this cycle: @QianyeSu · @TyceHerrman · @hawkff · @jsiu93 · @reorx · @md786-dotcom · @OPesicka · @dominionthedev.\n\n### Mole Mac App\n\nPrefer a GUI? [Mole Mac App](https://mole.fit/) brings cleaning, app management, maintenance, disk analysis, and live system status into one native app, with review before deletion and a customizable menu bar HUD. It is $19 once, with lifetime updates and a 14-day refund. [Download and try it](https://mole.fit/download). The CLI stays free and open source.\n",
